{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, Anti-MRSA", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: First AMP from the Australia marsupial discovered via sequence homology search. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (38.71%) to Saha-CATH5 G:19%; R: 16%; I:13%. Mol. Wt: 3548.255; GRAVY: -0.22; Mol Formula: C159H258N53O35S2; mol ex coeff: 5675. Activity: in cation-adjusted Mueller Hinton Broth, active against P-aeruginosa ATCC27853 (MIC>64 ug/ml), E. coli ATCC25922 (MIC 16-64 ug/ml), S. aureus MRSA (8-16 ug/ml), S-pneumoniae ATCC49619 (MIC>64 ug/ml), S. pyogenes ATCC19615 (MIC 64 ug/ml), S. agalactiae ATCC12386 (MIC 64 ug/ml), S-dysgalactiae (MIC>64 ug/ml), S-lutetiensis (MIC>64 ug/ml), S-equi (MIC>64 ug/ml), S-oralis (MIC>64 ug/ml), S. salivarius (MIC 64 ug/ml), S. mutans (MIC>64 ug/ml), L. monocytogenes (MIC 64 ug/ml), P-multocida (MIC>64 ug/ml), K-pneumoniae (MIC >64 ug/ml), C. parapsilosis ATCC 22019 (MIC 32 ug/ml), C. krusei ATCC 6258 (MIC 64 ug/ml), C-glabrata (MIC >64 ug/ml), and C-albicans (MIC >64 ug/ml). In addition, PhciCath5 inactivated C. pecorum IPTaLE and MarsBar elementary bodies and significantly reduced the number of inclusions compared to the control (p<0.0001). Antimicrobial robustness: 20% whole murine blood-sensitive E. coli (MIC >175 ug/ml). MIC is also cation-sensitive:E. coli ATCC25922 (MHB cation), cation-insensitive:S. aureus ATCC29213 (MHB cation). Updated Jan2026", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "33852625", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS One. 2021 Apr 14;16(4):e0249658. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0249658. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03601", "source_id": "AP03601", "source_numeric_id": "03601", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03601", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Koala cathelicidin PhciCath5 has antimicrobial activity, including against Chlamydia pecorum.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
